-**Edge Cases and Pitfalls**
-Not given in the sources.
+**Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
+-   **Zero at Lattice Points:** The noise value is exactly zero at every integer lattice point, causing undesired artifacts in amplitude distribution [S3].
+-   **Anisotropy:** Perlin noise exhibits undesired axis-aligned anisotropy caused by correlation in the hash function, visible as horizontal features in the periodogram [S3].
+-   **Band-pass Limitation:** Perlin noise is only weakly band-pass, which may lead to aliasing and detail loss compared to other noise functions [S3].
+-   **Gradient Selection:** The gradients are selected from the 12 vectors defined by the directions from the center of a cube to its edges [S3].
